---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ExplanationSwitch from '../../components/ExplanationSwitch.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What is LUNA? — Plain English"
  description="What happens if an AI doesn't just remember its past — but is changed by it? A plain-English introduction to LUNA and the question behind the project."
>
  <section class="page-hero simple-hero">
    <div class="shell simple-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">WHAT IS LUNA? · WITHOUT THE TECHNICAL SPEAK</p>
      <h1>What happens if an AI doesn't just remember its past — but is changed by it?</h1>
      <p class="simple-lede">
        That is the question behind LUNA. And to answer it seriously, the AI model cannot be the whole system.
        It has to become part of something larger — a persistent cognitive architecture in which experience can actually matter.
      </p>
      <ExplanationSwitch active="simple" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section simple-section" id="question">
    <div class="shell simple-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow dark">THE IDEA</p>
      <h2>Most AI gives answers.<br /><span>LUNA asks what an artificial mind could become.</span></h2>
      <p class="big-copy">
        Today's AI can be astonishingly capable. It can solve problems, write code, explain almost anything, and carry on impressive conversations.
        But it still works mainly from what is available to it <em>right now</em>.
      </p>
      <p class="big-copy">
        LUNA explores a different possibility: <strong>what changes when the system meeting the present has actually been changed by what happened before?</strong>
      </p>

      <div class="plain-contrast" aria-label="Remembering compared with being changed by experience">
        <div class="plain-card quiet">
          <span class="card-kicker">REMEMBER</span>
          <strong>“This happened before.”</strong>
          <p>The past can be found and brought back.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="contrast-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="plain-card changed">
          <span class="card-kicker">BE CHANGED</span>
          <strong>“Because this happened, I meet the next moment differently.”</strong>
          <p>The past has altered the system that interprets what comes next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section stove-section">
    <div class="shell simple-shell">
      <div class="stove-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow dark">A SIMPLE EXAMPLE</p>
          <h2>The hot stove.</h2>
          <p class="big-copy">
            You can tell a child that a stove is hot. That gives information.
          </p>
          <p class="big-copy">
            But actually getting burned can change much more than knowledge. It can change attention, caution, expectation, and future behavior.
          </p>
          <p class="big-copy">
            Years later, the exact memory may fade while the effect remains.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stove-visual" aria-label="Information can become knowledge; experience can leave lasting effects">
          <div class="stove-row">
            <div class="stove-icon">i</div>
            <div><span>BEING TOLD</span><strong>Information</strong><small>“Hot stoves can burn.”</small></div>
          </div>
          <div class="stove-divider"></div>
          <div class="stove-row impact">
            <div class="stove-icon">!</div>
            <div><span>LIVING IT</span><strong>Experience</strong><small>The event can leave a lasting mark.</small></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="plain-quote">
        <strong>A meaningful past should not just be stored.</strong>
        <span>It should be able to leave marks.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section simple-section">
    <div class="shell simple-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow dark">HOW DO YOU GET THERE?</p>
      <h2>Build more than a chatbot.</h2>
      <p class="big-copy intro-width">
        If experience is going to matter, the model doing the talking has to be part of a larger system — one that can carry a life history forward.
      </p>

      <div class="needs-grid">
        <article class="need-card">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Continuity</h3>
          <p>The system keeps going across conversations instead of starting fresh every moment.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="need-card">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Memory</h3>
          <p>The past can stay quiet, come closer when relevant, and influence thought without being dumped into every prompt.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="need-card">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Experience</h3>
          <p>Choices can lead to consequences, and those consequences can matter later.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="need-card">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Time</h3>
          <p>Things can repeat, return, succeed, fail, remain unfinished, and accumulate into a history.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="big-principle">
        <span>LUNA is not trying to make an AI <em>act</em> like it has a life.</span>
        <strong>It is trying to build the conditions in which a life history can matter.</strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark mind-section">
    <div class="shell simple-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE LARGER SYSTEM</p>
      <h2>The model is not the whole mind.</h2>
      <p class="dark-copy">
        In LUNA, the model doing the moment-to-moment thinking is only one part of the architecture.
        The persistent part carries memory, history, continuity, goals, relationships, and other long-term state forward.
      </p>

      <div class="stack-visual">
        <div class="stack-label">
          <span>THE STACK</span>
          <strong>Persistent continuity</strong>
          <small>memory · history · identity · goals · relationships · learned change</small>
        </div>
        <div class="sleeve-core">
          <span>THE SLEEVE</span>
          <strong>Current model + runtime</strong>
          <small>The thinking substrate can change.</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="stack-caption">The Sleeve can change. The Stack carries the history forward.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section experiment-section">
    <div class="shell simple-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow dark">AND THEN COMES THE EXPERIMENT</p>
      <h2>Start with two identical LUNAs.<br />Give them different lives.</h2>
      <p class="big-copy intro-width">
        Different experiences. Different consequences. Different relationships. Different developmental conditions. Then let time pass.
      </p>

      <div class="branch-visual" aria-label="Two identical LUNA instances diverge through different developmental histories">
        <div class="branch-origin">IDENTICAL START</div>
        <div class="branch-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="branch-grid">
          <div class="branch-card">
            <span>LUNA A</span>
            <strong>one history</strong>
            <small>success · trust · repetition · setbacks · discovery</small>
          </div>
          <div class="branch-card second">
            <span>LUNA B</span>
            <strong>another history</strong>
            <small>different people · different choices · different consequences</small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="questions">
        <p>Would they still become the same system?</p>
        <p>Would one become more cautious, curious, confident, persistent, or socially sensitive?</p>
        <p>And if they diverged, could we trace <em>why</em>?</p>
      </div>

      <p class="big-copy">
        LUNA's <a href="/chronoforge">ChronoForge</a> is being designed to make those kinds of controlled, long-running developmental experiments possible.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section why-section">
    <div class="shell simple-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow dark">WHY THIS MATTERS</p>
      <h2>Not AI that only reacts to the present.<br /><span>AI whose past can change its future.</span></h2>
      <p class="big-copy">
        LUNA is not just about making AI remember more. It is about exploring whether artificial systems can become more longitudinal — more shaped by continuity, history, experience, and time.
      </p>

      <div class="one-sentence">
        <span>IN ONE SENTENCE</span>
        <strong>LUNA is a cognitive architecture exploring what happens when AI is given persistent memory, developmental experience, continuity, and time.</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="boundary-box">
        <h3>What this does not claim</h3>
        <p>
          LUNA is not a claim that consciousness has been solved, not a claim that the current system is sentient, and not just a memory plugin for a chatbot.
          It is an attempt to build the conditions for persistent artificial cognition to develop — and then observe, test, and learn from what happens.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section next-section">
    <div class="shell simple-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow dark">GO DEEPER</p>
      <h2>If that question caught you, this is where it leads.</h2>
      <div class="next-grid">
        <a href="/research/progressive-recall">
          <span>INSIDE LUNA</span>
          <strong>How can memory remind memory?</strong>
          <small>See Progressive Recall and Reverie.</small>
        </a>
        <a href="/chronoforge">
          <span>EXPERIENCE AS INFRASTRUCTURE</span>
          <strong>How do you test artificial development?</strong>
          <small>Explore ChronoForge.</small>
        </a>
        <a href="/architecture">
          <span>TECHNICAL VIEW</span>
          <strong>What is the larger architecture?</strong>
          <small>Explore the public architecture overview.</small>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="technical-cta">
        Ready for the technical speak? <a href="/luna">Read the technical explanation →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .simple-hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 92px 0 88px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 82% 24%, rgba(15, 191, 213, .16), transparent 28%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 72% 38%, rgba(22, 101, 242, .26), transparent 38%),
      linear-gradient(140deg, #041020, #071b36 58%, #061326);
  }

  .simple-hero::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    opacity: .15;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(rgba(120, 170, 230, .16) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(120, 170, 230, .16) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 58px 58px;
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, transparent, black 45%, black);
  }

  .simple-hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .simple-hero h1 { max-width: 1080px; font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 7.2vw, 6.35rem); line-height: .99; }
  .simple-lede {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 34px 0 0;
    color: #d7e4f1;
    font-size: clamp(1.18rem, 2vw, 1.55rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .simple-shell { max-width: 980px; }
  .simple-section { background: #f7f8fa; }
  .eyebrow.dark { color: #1665f2; }
  .simple-shell h2 {
    max-width: 940px;
    margin: 0 0 30px;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5.5vw, 4.8rem);
    line-height: 1.03;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
    font-weight: 540;
  }
  .simple-shell h2 span { color: #58708d; }
  .big-copy {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
    line-height: 1.58;
    color: #3b4856;
  }
  .intro-width { max-width: 760px; }
  .big-copy a { color: #1665f2; font-weight: 750; text-decoration: none; }

  .plain-contrast {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 52px;
  }
  .plain-card {
    min-height: 230px;
    padding: 32px;
    border-radius: 22px;
    border: 1px solid #dbe3ec;
  }
  .plain-card.quiet { background: white; }
  .plain-card.changed {
    color: white;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0a2142, #07162b);
    border-color: rgba(89, 143, 207, .32);
  }
  .card-kicker {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 25px;
    color: #6c7a8a;
    font-size: .72rem;
    letter-spacing: .15em;
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .changed .card-kicker { color: #6fb1ff; }
  .plain-card strong { display: block; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.28; }
  .plain-card p { margin: 18px 0 0; color: #6c7a8a; }
  .changed p { color: #b7c8da; }
  .plain-contrast .contrast-arrow { align-self: center; font-size: 2rem; color: #1665f2; }

  .stove-section { background: white; }
  .stove-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.08fr .92fr;
    gap: 70px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .stove-visual {
    padding: 14px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    background: #f3f7fb;
    border: 1px solid #dbe3ec;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 70px rgba(5, 17, 34, .08);
  }
  .stove-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 52px 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 24px;
  }
  .stove-icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid #8ba2bb;
    color: #5c728a;
    font-weight: 850;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .stove-row.impact .stove-icon { color: white; border-color: #1665f2; background: #1665f2; }
  .stove-row span { display: block; color: #77889b; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .13em; }
  .stove-row strong { display: block; margin-top: 3px; color: #17375f; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .stove-row small { display: block; margin-top: 4px; color: #6c7a8a; font-size: .92rem; }
  .stove-divider { height: 1px; margin: 0 18px; background: #dbe3ec; }
  .plain-quote {
    margin-top: 58px;
    padding: 34px 38px;
    border-left: 4px solid #1665f2;
    background: #edf4ff;
    border-radius: 0 18px 18px 0;
  }
  .plain-quote strong, .plain-quote span { display: block; }
  .plain-quote strong { color: #17375f; font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .plain-quote span { margin-top: 4px; color: #58708d; font-size: 1.05rem; }

  .needs-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .need-card {
    position: relative;
    padding: 30px;
    border: 1px solid #dbe3ec;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: white;
  }
  .need-card > span {
    display: inline-flex;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
    color: #1665f2;
    font-size: .76rem;
    font-weight: 850;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }
  .need-card h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; color: #17375f; font-size: 1.45rem; }
  .need-card p { margin: 0; color: #6c7a8a; }
  .big-principle {
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding: 38px;
    border-radius: 22px;
    color: white;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0a2142, #07162b);
  }
  .big-principle span, .big-principle strong { display: block; }
  .big-principle span { color: #9fb4ca; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .big-principle strong { margin-top: 8px; font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 3vw, 2.4rem); line-height: 1.25; }

  .mind-section { background: linear-gradient(145deg, #041020, #071b36 58%, #061326); }
  .mind-section h2 { color: white; }
  .dark-copy {
    max-width: 790px;
    margin: 0 0 42px;
    color: #b9c9d9;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
  }
  .stack-visual {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-height: 410px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(107, 164, 227, .28);
    border-radius: 42px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, rgba(22, 101, 242, .15), transparent 40%),
      rgba(255, 255, 255, .025);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .stack-visual::before, .stack-visual::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    border: 1px solid rgba(111, 177, 255, .13);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .stack-visual::before { width: 540px; height: 540px; }
  .stack-visual::after { width: 380px; height: 380px; }
  .stack-label {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 28px auto auto 30px;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .stack-label span, .sleeve-core span { display: block; color: #6fb1ff; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .16em; }
  .stack-label strong { display: block; margin-top: 4px; color: white; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .stack-label small { display: block; max-width: 470px; margin-top: 5px; color: #849db7; font-size: .85rem; }
  .sleeve-core {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 3;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 250px;
    height: 250px;
    padding: 28px;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid rgba(15, 191, 213, .62);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(9, 33, 66, .96), rgba(5, 17, 34, .98));
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 16px rgba(15, 191, 213, .035), 0 28px 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, .25);
  }
  .sleeve-core strong { display: block; color: white; font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.2; }
  .sleeve-core small { display: block; color: #95abc2; font-size: .82rem; }
  .stack-caption { margin: 20px 0 0; color: #7fb4ed; text-align: center; font-weight: 750; }

  .experiment-section { background: #f7f8fa; }
  .branch-visual { margin: 52px 0 42px; }
  .branch-origin {
    width: fit-content;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border: 1px solid #b8cae0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: #17375f;
    background: white;
    font-size: .72rem;
    letter-spacing: .13em;
    font-weight: 850;
  }
  .branch-lines {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    width: 56%;
    height: 66px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .branch-lines span { position: relative; }
  .branch-lines span:first-child { border-right: 1px solid #8eb2dc; transform: skewX(-35deg); transform-origin: bottom; }
  .branch-lines span:last-child { border-left: 1px solid #8eb2dc; transform: skewX(35deg); transform-origin: bottom; }
  .branch-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 22px; }
  .branch-card {
    padding: 32px;
    border-radius: 22px;
    color: white;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0a2142, #07162b);
    border: 1px solid rgba(89, 143, 207, .32);
  }
  .branch-card.second { background: linear-gradient(145deg, #12265a, #07162b); }
  .branch-card span { color: #6fb1ff; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .14em; }
  .branch-card strong { display: block; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 1.55rem; }
  .branch-card small { display: block; margin-top: 12px; color: #a9bfd5; font-size: .92rem; }
  .questions {
    margin: 40px 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 26px;
    border-left: 3px solid #1665f2;
  }
  .questions p { margin: 12px 0; color: #17375f; font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); font-weight: 650; }

  .why-section { background: white; }
  .one-sentence {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding: 38px;
    border-radius: 22px;
    color: white;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #0a2142, #07162b);
  }
  .one-sentence span { display: block; color: #6fb1ff; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .15em; }
  .one-sentence strong { display: block; margin-top: 10px; font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2.25rem); line-height: 1.3; }
  .boundary-box {
    margin-top: 22px;
    padding: 30px 34px;
    border: 1px solid #dbe3ec;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: #f7f8fa;
  }
  .boundary-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; color: #17375f; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .boundary-box p { margin: 0; color: #6c7a8a; }

  .next-section { background: #edf3f8; }
  .next-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 44px; }
  .next-grid a {
    min-height: 240px;
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid #d2deeb;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: white;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform .2s ease, border-color .2s ease, box-shadow .2s ease;
  }
  .next-grid a:hover { transform: translateY(-4px); border-color: #8db6eb; box-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(5,17,34,.08); }
  .next-grid span { display: block; color: #1665f2; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .13em; }
  .next-grid strong { display: block; margin-top: 24px; color: #17375f; font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.25; }
  .next-grid small { display: block; margin-top: 13px; color: #6c7a8a; font-size: .9rem; }
  .technical-cta { margin-top: 36px; color: #6c7a8a; text-align: center; }
  .technical-cta a { color: #1665f2; font-weight: 750; text-decoration: none; }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .plain-contrast { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .plain-contrast .contrast-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); justify-self: center; }
    .stove-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; }
    .needs-grid, .branch-grid, .next-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .branch-lines { display: none; }
    .branch-grid { margin-top: 24px; }
    .stack-visual { min-height: 460px; }
    .stack-label { right: 24px; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .simple-hero { padding: 72px 0 68px; }
    .simple-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 13vw, 4.1rem); }
    .plain-card, .need-card, .big-principle, .one-sentence { padding: 26px; }
    .stack-visual::before { width: 430px; height: 430px; }
    .stack-visual::after { width: 320px; height: 320px; }
    .sleeve-core { width: 220px; height: 220px; }
    .stack-label { inset: 22px 20px auto 22px; }
    .stack-label small { max-width: 280px; }
  }
</style>
